## Work ids — never mint a `CHG-NNN` locally

A change id is allocated in `nous.db` **before** it appears in a readiness
artifact, a commit message, or a feedback event. Ask the operator for one:
`nous_trace.py change next --project <id> --reserve --title "…"` (prints the next
free id for this project and creates the row).

CHG ids are **project-scoped and substrate-allocated**. An id you pick yourself
may be the one the operator allocates to a different change the same day, and
until it is registered the work behind it is invisible to `nous.db`. The
`[CHG Id Provenance]` drift section names every unregistered id used here.

The CHG narrative lives in `nous.db` and is delivered as
`docs/stories/CHANGES.md`; don't maintain a parallel `docs/changes/*.md`.
Full guide: `docs/dev-guide/SPECS.md`.

